                      (    forth6809.asm):12797         ; TSTDOTQUOTE - unit test for .". No STATE check at all in its
                      (    forth6809.asm):12798         ; own code (confirmed by reading it directly - matches "no
                      (    forth6809.asm):12799         ; interpretation semantics, per ANS" without a specific -14
                      (    forth6809.asm):12800         ; throw, unlike [CHAR]/S"), so only the compiling case is
                      (    forth6809.asm):12801         ; tested, matching how it's actually meant to be used. Its own
                      (    forth6809.asm):12802         ; runtime (DOTSTR) calls TYPE internally, which has two entirely
                      (    forth6809.asm):12803         ; different implementations gated by SERIALPOLL (the same real
                      (    forth6809.asm):12804         ; finding from section 3.1) - applying that lesson from the
                      (    forth6809.asm):12805         ; start here rather than re-discovering it: EMITCH works
                      (    forth6809.asm):12806         ; universally for a single-character check, but this outputs
