                      (    forth6809.asm):15431         ; Comments test harness (glossary section 3.16). Both words
                      (    forth6809.asm):15432         ; parse from source, so both redirect SRCADDR/SRCLEN/TOIN,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15433         ; matching the established pattern from sections 3.8-3.12.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15434         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):15435         ; ( specifically carries real bug-fix history worth verifying
                      (    forth6809.asm):15436         ; directly, not just noting: a prior version omitted consuming
                      (    forth6809.asm):15437         ; WORD's own returned c-addr, leaving a stray value on the data
                      (    forth6809.asm):15438         ; stack after every "(...)" comment - confirmed via MAME at the
                      (    forth6809.asm):15439         ; time, symptomatic both as a visible stray value in interpret
                      (    forth6809.asm):15440         ; mode and as a -22 CSP mismatch for any colon definition
                      (    forth6809.asm):15441         ; containing one. This section's own test specifically confirms
                      (    forth6809.asm):15442         ; the data stack is genuinely unchanged (net 0), not just that
                      (    forth6809.asm):15443         ; parsing advanced correctly.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15444         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):15445         
                      (    forth6809.asm):15446         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):15447         ; TSTLPAREN - unit test for (. Fake source "hi)m" with TOIN
                      (    forth6809.asm):15448         ; starting at 0 - verifies TOIN lands exactly past the closing
                      (    forth6809.asm):15449         ; paren (at 3, immediately before "m", not consuming it), and
                      (    forth6809.asm):15450         ; that the data stack is genuinely unchanged - the specific
                      (    forth6809.asm):15451         ; behavior the bug-fix comment describes as previously broken.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15452         ; Since ( only ever advances TOIN, never SRCADDR itself, the
                      (    forth6809.asm):15453         ; fake source's own known address (TSTNAMEB) is used directly to
                      (    forth6809.asm):15454         ; verify the character just past the paren, with no need to
                      (    forth6809.asm):15455         ; re-read SRCADDR after the call.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15456         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
C324                  (    forth6809.asm):15457         TSTLPAREN: LDD  SRCADDR
                      (    forth6809.asm):15458                    STD  TSTSASAV
                      (    forth6809.asm):15459                    LDD  SRCLEN
                      (    forth6809.asm):15460                    STD  TSTSLSAV
                      (    forth6809.asm):15461                    LDD  TOIN
                      (    forth6809.asm):15462                    STD  TSTTISAV
                      (    forth6809.asm):15463         
