                      (    forth6809.asm):15649         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):15650         ; Environmental & System Queries test harness (glossary section
                      (    forth6809.asm):15651         ; 3.17). Five words (TIB/#TIB/>IN/SPAN/BL) are simple constant/
                      (    forth6809.asm):15652         ; variable readers, combined into one test rather than five
                      (    forth6809.asm):15653         ; separate ones, matching the established approach from section
                      (    forth6809.asm):15654         ; 3.14's own TSTBASE.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15655         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):15656         ; REFILL genuinely blocks on real input when the source is the
                      (    forth6809.asm):15657         ; terminal (confirmed by reading its own code directly: the
                      (    forth6809.asm):15658         ; terminal branch calls QUERY, which - per section 3.1's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):15659         ; already-established finding - calls ACCEPT, which calls KEY,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15660         ; which spins forever without real input). Only its safely-
                      (    forth6809.asm):15661         ; testable path (source is a string, SRCID<>0) is tested here,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15662         ; matching the same reasoning already applied to KEY/ACCEPT/
                      (    forth6809.asm):15663         ; EXPECT/QUERY themselves in section 3.1.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15664         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):15665         ; EVALUATE genuinely executes its given string as real Forth
                      (    forth6809.asm):15666         ; source via JSR INTERPRET - confirmed via INTERPRET's own code
                      (    forth6809.asm):15667         ; that it simply stops and returns when input is exhausted (no
                      (    forth6809.asm):15668         ; automatic REFILL, so no blocking risk), making a short,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15669         ; deliberately harmless string ("1 2 +") safe to evaluate
                      (    forth6809.asm):15670         ; directly.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15671         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):15672         ; ENVIRONMENT? carries substantial, already-documented bug-fix
                      (    forth6809.asm):15673         ; history (a COMPAREW-clobbers-X bug, confirmed via MAME with the
                      (    forth6809.asm):15674         ; exact $4E4D symptom - reading two bytes of the NEXT table
                      (    forth6809.asm):15675         ; entry's own name text as if they were the current entry's
                      (    forth6809.asm):15676         ; value). This section's own tests specifically query
                      (    forth6809.asm):15677         ; "/COUNTED-STRING" immediately followed by "MAX-N" - the exact
                      (    forth6809.asm):15678         ; adjacent pair the bug-fix comment describes - so a regression
                      (    forth6809.asm):15679         ; of that specific mechanism would be caught again, not just
                      (    forth6809.asm):15680         ; assumed fixed from the comment alone.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15681         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):15682         
                      (    forth6809.asm):15683         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):15684         ; TSTENVVARS - combined unit test for TIB, #TIB, >IN, SPAN, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):15685         ; BL. The first four are variables (return their own address);
                      (    forth6809.asm):15686         ; BL is a constant (returns 32 directly).
                      (    forth6809.asm):15687         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
