C354 BDC3C5           (    forth6809.asm):16330                    JSR   TSTWORDS
C357 BDC447           (    forth6809.asm):16331                    JSR   TSTDUMP
                      (    forth6809.asm):16332         
                      (    forth6809.asm):16333                    ENDC ; <<<<
                      (    forth6809.asm):16334         
C35A 39               (    forth6809.asm):16335                    RTS
                      (    forth6809.asm):16336         
C35B 546F6F6C73       (    forth6809.asm):16337         TSTTOOLSMSG: FCC "Tools"
                      (    forth6809.asm):16338         
                      (    forth6809.asm):16339                    IFEQ TSTSELECTOR-17  ; >>>>
                      (    forth6809.asm):16340         
                      (    forth6809.asm):16341         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):16342         ; Tools test harness (glossary section 3.18). WORDS depends
                      (    forth6809.asm):16343         ; directly on LATEST (confirmed via its own code: it walks from
                      (    forth6809.asm):16344         ; LATEST until the chain terminates at 0) - the same real, pre-
                      (    forth6809.asm):16345         ; COLD dependency section 3.17's own TSTEVALUATE was found to
                      (    forth6809.asm):16346         ; need, so this section's own WORDS test redirects LATEST too,
                      (    forth6809.asm):16347         ; applying that lesson from the start rather than rediscovering
                      (    forth6809.asm):16348         ; it. All three words produce visible output, so all apply the
                      (    forth6809.asm):16349         ; SERIALPOLL-conditional split established in section 3.1.
                      (    forth6809.asm):16350         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):16351         ; .S prints the ENTIRE real data stack, including whatever this
                      (    forth6809.asm):16352         ; whole calling chain (TSTRUNNER and everything above it) already
                      (    forth6809.asm):16353         ; left there before this test even started - unlike every other
                      (    forth6809.asm):16354         ; test in this session, there's no way to know the full, exact
                      (    forth6809.asm):16355         ; output in advance. This test's own verification is deliberately
                      (    forth6809.asm):16356         ; narrower as a result: confirms the core, documented guarantee
                      (    forth6809.asm):16357         ; directly (the stack is genuinely unchanged afterward, non-
                      (    forth6809.asm):16358         ; destructive for real) plus, in interrupt mode only (where the
                      (    forth6809.asm):16359         ; first characters queued are unambiguously this test's own top
                      (    forth6809.asm):16360         ; value, since .S starts from the current top of stack), that the
                      (    forth6809.asm):16361         ; very first characters match - rather than attempting to predict
                      (    forth6809.asm):16362         ; or verify the complete printed output.
                      (    forth6809.asm):16363         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):16364         ; DUMP carries real, already-documented bug-fix history: a prior
                      (    forth6809.asm):16365         ; version's ASCII column read past the actual byte count on a
                      (    forth6809.asm):16366         ; partial final line, showing garbage characters for the unused
                      (    forth6809.asm):16367         ; portion - fixed via DUVALID tracking. This section's own test
                      (    forth6809.asm):16368         ; specifically dumps a non-multiple-of-16 byte count (5), the
                      (    forth6809.asm):16369         ; exact scenario that bug affected, verifying the ASCII column's
                      (    forth6809.asm):16370         ; own blanking for the remaining, invalid columns.
                      (    forth6809.asm):16371         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
