EA02 39               (    forth6809.asm):19910         UNLOOP:  RTS             ; DESIGN CHANGE: was PULS X/LEAS 6,S/PSHS X/RTS
                      (    forth6809.asm):19911                                   ; (a real discard of the loop-control frame).
                      (    forth6809.asm):19912                                   ; EXIT's own EXITUNLOOP mechanism already
                      (    forth6809.asm):19913                                   ; discards the frame automatically and
                      (    forth6809.asm):19914                                   ; correctly on every path - traced and
                      (    forth6809.asm):19915                                   ; confirmed: with no enclosing DO (compiled
                      (    forth6809.asm):19916                                   ; count 0), with one enclosing DO and no
                      (    forth6809.asm):19917                                   ; prior UNLOOP (discards the full 8-byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):19918                                   ; frame correctly). The one combination that
                      (    forth6809.asm):19919                                   ; broke was UNLOOP immediately before EXIT -
                      (    forth6809.asm):19920                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):19921                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):19922                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):19923                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):19924                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):19925                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):19926                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):19927                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):19928                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):19929                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):19930                                   ; a second, conflicting discard mechanism.
                      (    forth6809.asm):19931         
